      "purposeInStoryline": "This is the opening lesson of the unit and the first half of the experimental-probability work. Learners meet Kamau's matatu tally notebook, surface their own misconceptions about predictability, and generate the central puzzle that drives every later lesson: why can careful records still not predict one trip? They compute Kamau's first experimental probability and open the Driving Question Board and the cumulative probability model. Lesson 2 tests the same ideas with a coin the learners toss themselves.",
