        "teacherMoves": "1. Say: 'Open your model to the two-stop tree. Today it answers new questions.'\n2. Circulate for 3 minutes while learners annotate. Check (i) the conditions box uses the right end branches, (ii) the four products are in a small sum-check box, (iii) early finishers' road-safety tree is labelled.\n3. If a learner's end branches do not sum to 1, say quietly: 'Your tree is telling you something is wrong. What does the sum give you?'\n4. With about 1 minute left: 'Compare with your partner. Point to ONE number where you differ. Whose is correct, and how do you know?' Cold-call 1 learner to read their Model Update Statement. Close: 'Next lesson we bring everything together to advise Kamau.'",
