    "teacherReflection": "After the lesson, reflect on the following:\n1. PREDICTION SPREAD: How many learners predicted a value below 16/25 for 'at least one'? What does that tell you about how they read 'at least one'?\n2. WHICH BRANCHES: Did pairs choose the right end branches for 'at least one' and 'exactly one'? Which pairs included E₁E₂ or left out F₁F₂?\n3. CIVIC ENGAGEMENT: Did the road-safety scenario generate genuine discussion, or did learners treat it as a routine calculation? If engagement was low, consider opening Lesson 11 with a real Nairobi road-safety statistic from the National Transport and Safety Authority (NTSA) to ground the mathematics in lived reality.\n4. INDEPENDENCE NOTE: Did learners grasp that the road-safety tree is not an independent tree (2/5 versus 1/10)? How did you handle the question of whether the multiplication still works?\n5. DQB QUALITY: Read the 'OPEN' question cards from today's DQB journal entries tonight. Which confusions are most common? Use the top two to write the opening retrieval question for Lesson 11.\n6. MODEL COMPLETENESS: How many models had the conditions box with correct values without teacher intervention? Target: at least 80% of learners.",
