      "knowledge": "Learners will know that: (i) a fair game requires each player to have an equal theoretical probability of winning, and fairness is verified by computing P(player wins) for all players and confirming equality; (ii) results from a short run of play can differ from theory, and the difference shrinks as the number of rounds grows (Law of Large Numbers); (iii) the full probability framework connects the experimental and theoretical sides of probability with the laws and tree diagrams.",
