        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Let us return to our Driving Question Board. Today we answer the questions.' Hand each group three colour-coded dot stickers. 'Read the questions. Decide: fully answered, partially answered, or needed rephrasing? Dot each one. Then pick ONE question, write the full answer on a new sticky note citing the lesson and the concept, and post it.' [3 minutes group work.] Cold-call 1 group to read one green-dotted question and its answer, then ask: 'Which lesson answered this? What was the key idea?' Point to the original driving question: 'Why can Kamau not know for certain whether the next seat will be filled, yet we can say something mathematical and useful about his chances? Thumbs up if our board now answers this.' Cold-call 1 student to state the answer in their own words. Photograph the final board.",
